# (after 0520) nvn/memory + frame step: shader-code pools stay out of the raw pool table, guest-file pages are wired before the residency commit, late 30 fps frames paced (Ocarina of Time)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/9143b6ff6217e491c8a3bffe3816d8178c5072e0  ("nvn: keep shader-code pools out of gmem_map, pre-wire guest files, and pace late 30 fps frames (PR #1971)")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-23 00:08 +0800; Co-authored-by: Stan Bono, uncraftablexd
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why (measured upstream, Ocarina of Time on an 8 GB iPhone 17, 30 fps cap, Kokiri Forest): 223 shader-code pools (317 MB) were resident and wired in the raw pool table for nothing
#   (the GPU never reads translated shaders' code), starving the guest's file-backed pages: 14-17 fps, 6,000-15,600 page-ins every 10 s. With the change: page-ins 100-400 per 10 s,
#   27-30 fps (upstream docs/reference/memory.md, PR #1971). The residency commit also paged guest files in from the GPU driver's wiring path, which froze once on an APFS lock (M1 iPad).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c, nvn_mtl.m, nvn_mtl.h, nvn_fstep.h; tests t_addr_known, t_file_wire, t_fstep, t_present_crop, t_present_rescue):
#   - nvnMemoryPoolGetBufferAddress no longer marks a non-virtual SHADER_CODE pool addressed (a buffer made in it, or a pointer scan, still does);
#   - a shared buffer on file pages (DM_GUEST_FILE) joining the residency set is mlock'ed outside g_res_mu before its change is queued and munlock'ed after res_commit_retiring;
#   - present_shape matches the window crop's aspect first when DM_SCREEN_ASPECT is set;
#   - frame step: idle-GPU start-up late frames do not raise the hold, unpaced holds whose GPU work fits a shorter one are probed, and an automatic 30 fps link switches to 60 Hz at
#     latency 2 when frames are late at hold 2 (an explicit DM_PRESENT_LINK or DM_PRESENT_LATENCY is honoured).
# Adapted: the res_add hunk (file wire) rejected and was redone by hand: this tree's res_add_at adds the heap in place of a placed resource instead of recursing, so the wire is taken on
#   that resource (a heap is never a shared buffer, so only plain shared buffers are wired, as upstream). Its Makefile hunk by hand. dm/games/0400486024DEC000/smoke.tsv (a Mac route) not taken.
#   The frame-step hunks apply beside 0503's DM_FPS_PAYBACK (nopay): with payback off a late frame's debt is still let go.
# Games: Ocarina of Time (0400486024DEC000); every game for the shader-code pools and the file wire. Switches: none new (DM_GUEST_FILE, DM_SCREEN_ASPECT, DM_PRESENT_LINK, DM_PRESENT_LATENCY exist).
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_addr_known 25, t_file_wire 12, t_fstep (all its checks), t_present_crop 126, t_present_rescue 113; all in HOST_TESTS.
# NOT measured here: the page-ins, wired memory and frame rate on an iPhone (the numbers above are upstream's).
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0520, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

